  "names": {
    "order": "given family",
    "conventions": "Given name then family name. Lithuanian surnames change with gender and marriage: the family list gives the male form (Kazlauskas, Butkus, Kairys). A married woman's form ends in -ienė (Kazlauskienė); an unmarried woman's ends in -aitė from -as (Kazlauskaitė), -ūtė from -us (Butkutė), or -ytė from -is and -ys (Kairytė). Since 2003 women may also use the neutral -ė form (Kazlauskė). Given names are gendered too: men's end in -as, -is, -us, women's in -a or -ė. Vilnius Poles use Polish names (women's -ski becomes -ska), and Russian, Belarusian and Ukrainian names in Lithuanian documents get Lithuanian endings (Ivanovas) while people use the plain form day to day.",
